llenger", "No public general-election polling to refine the estimate"], "rationale": "The R+10 district, incumbent McClintock's 2-to-1 fundraising edge, and a unanimous Solid/Safe R consensus across ten raters all point to a comfortable Republican hold, and markets price Masuda's chances at only about 6 percent. The forecast settles near the rating consensus at roughly R+13, with Masuda's active campaign and debate presence keeping some residual uncertainty.", "watch": "Any late independent spending or polling showing Masuda consolidating Democratic and moderate turnout could narrow the margin, though an upset remains unlikely.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tom McClintock (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Tom McClintock seeks another term in this R+10 district covering the Sierra foothills and Central Valley. He advanced to the general against Democrat Michael Masuda, an engineer running a grassroots campaign focused on rural healthcare, wildfire and insurance issues. McClintock has raised about $1.25 million to Masuda's $580,000 and holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, with no outside spending on either side.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the seat Solid or Safe for Republicans, and prediction markets give Masuda only a small chance. The two met in several televised debates where local issues dominated, but no public polling exists to suggest the incumbent is vulnerable. The forecast expects McClintock to win by a wide, double-digit margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1154, "margin": -9.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1311, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0595, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0545, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0432, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin